  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:graphql",
  "domain": "infrastructure",
  "definition": "GraphQL is a query language and runtime for APIs in which clients specify exactly the data they need against a strongly typed schema, and the server returns precisely that shape in a single response. A single endpoint exposes a graph of types whose fields are resolved by server-side resolvers, eliminating the over-fetching and under-fetching common to fixed REST endpoints. GraphQL supports queries, mutations and subscriptions, and its self-describing schema enables strong tooling, introspection and client code generation.",
